# Playwright VRT baselines written by layout-vrt.spec.ts's toHaveScreenshot().
# Ignored, like the two artifact directories above, because nothing here is a
# reviewed reference: no storefront baseline has ever been tracked, so the
# spec writes one on first run and passes against itself — on a dev machine
# and in CI alike. Committing whichever branch happened to run last would
# silently promote that branch's rendering to the reference.
#
# Making VRT actually gate is worth doing deliberately: it needs baselines
# generated on the same platform CI renders on (the files are suffixed
# -chromium-linux) and a decision about which commit is "correct". Until
# then, treat layout-vrt as smoke coverage, not a visual gate.
*.spec.ts-snapshots/

# Audit run output — regenerated by `frontend-audit.spec.ts` on every run.
# The findings that matter live in docs/TNM-MENU-01/FRONTEND-AUDIT.md;
# committing the raw per-route JSON would churn on every environment.
e2e/audit-report/
